invariant: INV-14
file: handshake_parser_ee.c
catches: handshake_strict_webpki
reason: the server_certificate_type arm stops checking that the body
  ends at its one CertificateType, so a body of two octets parses on
  its first. RFC 7250 §4.2 permits a single value there, and RFC 9846
  §6 makes a body of the wrong length a decode_error.
  bin/handshake_strict_webpki's two-octet row objects.

--- old
    uint8_t type = rb_u8(&e);
    if (e.err || rb_left(&e) != 0) {
--- new
    uint8_t type = rb_u8(&e);
    if (e.err) {
